21. Schema Reference
A JSON Schema for validating .lw files should enforce:

The root object requires format, version, and instances

format must equal "lime-world"

version must match the pattern ^\d+\.\d+$

instances is an array of instance objects

Each instance object requires an instID string

Each instance may contain name, id, parent, properties, tags, attributes

parent is a dotted path string starting with a top-level container name

vec3 is an array of exactly three numbers

dims is an array of exactly two numbers

color is an array of exactly three integers between 0 and 255

Optional top-level objects (metadata, lighting, environment, camera, spawn, physics, assets) are plain objects

Applications may extend the schema with custom instance classes and property types.

22. Reserved Field Names
The following top-level field names are reserved and must not be used for custom data:

format, version, metadata, instances, lighting, environment, camera, spawn, physics, assets

The following instance-level field names are reserved:

instID, name, id, parent, properties, tags, attributes

The following container names are reserved and always exist:

workspace, replicated, server, interface, starter, server.storage, server.scripts, starter.character, starter.player, starter.gears

Custom data should live in attributes (per-instance) or in an application-specific top-level field prefixed with x- (e.g. x-myapp).

23. Differences from Roblox .rbxlx
Feature	Roblox .rbxlx	LiMe World .lw
Encoding	XML	JSON
Readability	Moderate	High
Diff-friendliness	Poor	Excellent
Script language	Luau	LMLua
Type encoding	Custom XML tags	JSON arrays and objects
Parenting	<Item> nesting	Dotted parent paths
Property storage	<Properties> block	properties object
Class identifier	<Item class="...">	instID field
Property naming	PascalCase	camelCase (main), PascalCase (sub)
Generic property names	No	Yes — resolved by instID
Top-level containers	Services	Implicit containers (workspace, server, etc.)
Binary variant	.rbxl	(planned: .lwb)
Schema	Proprietary	Open JSON Schema
Versioning	Roblox-managed	Semver string in-file
